   "title": "Test circuit for response time",
   "page": 12,
   "description": "A pulse drives the LED through a series resistor RD, with the cathode grounded. The phototransistor is a common-emitter stage: emitter to ground, collector pulled up to Vcc through RL, output taken at the collector. The output falls while the LED is on. td is the time from the input's rising edge to the output's 10 % point, tr from 10 % to 90 %; ts is the time from the input's falling edge back to the 90 % point, tf from 90 % to 10 %. The table's tr and tf are at VCE = 2 V, IC = 2 mA, RL = 100 Ω.",
